# Graphify — knowledge base + architecture search

This repo maintains a Graphify graph at `graphify-out/graph.json`
([Graphify](https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify)).

## When to use Graphify

Prefer Graphify for **cross-cutting** questions — architecture, dependency paths,
“what touches X”, how capabilities relate in code:

```bash
graphify query "<question>" --graph graphify-out/graph.json
graphify path "<A>" "<B>" --graph graphify-out/graph.json
graphify explain "<concept>" --graph graphify-out/graph.json
```

If a global multi-repo graph exists, use that path instead (see user/workspace Graphify config).

## When NOT to use Graphify first

Governance artifacts still go through the SDD surface (file read or `sdd serve` MCP):

- capability specs, plans, principles → `get_capability` / `get_plan` / `get_principles`
- findings lifecycle → `list_findings` / `search_findings` / `propose_finding`
- progress → `get_progress` / `record_progress`

Graphify complements those tools; it does not replace them.

## Keeping the graph fresh

- After meaningful code changes: `graphify update .` (AST only, no API key)
- After doc/wiki/PDF changes that should enter the graph: run `/graphify --update`
  (or `graphify extract .`) with a configured LLM backend
- If `graphify-out/graph.json` is missing: `graphify update .` before relying on queries
